WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.490
MAX: This week, we're talking
about Cloud Run, sea cables,

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:03.950
and managing your cloud.

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:06.550
I'm Max, and welcome to "This
Week in Cloud," where we serve

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:09.030
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:12.840
First up, a minor update, Cloud
Run is generally available.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.180
Cloud Run is a fully
managed serverless execution

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.640
environment that lets you
run stateless containers

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.903
without worrying
about infrastructure.

00:00:19.903 --> 00:00:21.570
We're pretty obsessed
with it over here,

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:22.820
and we hope you like it, too.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.210
So check out this
little product.

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.780
It might just make your day.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.530
Once you've fallen in
love with Cloud Run,

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.470
you may find yourself with
multiple cloud solutions.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:32.549
That's OK.

00:00:32.549 --> 00:00:34.950
It turns out, for many
enterprise networks,

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.520
it's complicated.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:39.210
Most businesses end up with
multi-cloud or hybrid cloud

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.480
and on-prem deployments.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.050
The Network
Intelligence Center was

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.342
designed to simplify things
for your network operations

00:00:45.342 --> 00:00:47.940
team by providing
comprehensive visibility

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.360
into your entire cloud strategy.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.330
As you scale that cloud
strategy, it's important to us

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:56.640
that you are only ever
charged for what you use,

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.550
and that you're using
exactly what you need.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:03.600
To help, the Budget API has
also been released to beta.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.730
The Budget API is designed
for managing budgets

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:08.220
programmatically at
scale, which is critical

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:11.400
when you have multiple budgets
across an organization.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.020
Try it out, and let us
know what you think.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.750
Subsea cables are literally
changing the world

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:21.980
by using a data pipe to bring
continents closer together,

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:24.390
metaphorically
speaking, of course.

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:27.890
The Curie cable is
10,500 kilometers long

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:29.930
and runs from the US to Chile.

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:31.430
And now that it's
operational, we're

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:34.400
starting on the first
branch to Panama.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.740
No matter where your
users are, Google Cloud

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:39.187
is here to help you reach them.

00:01:39.187 --> 00:01:41.270
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:43.770
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.980
Have any thoughts or ideas,
leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.540
We'll see you in the cloud.

